==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|status}}, from {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|statut}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|statutum||a statute}}, neuter singular of {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|statutus}}, past participle of {{m|la|statuō||I set up, establish}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈstætʃuːt/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# Written law, as laid down by the [[legislature]].
# {{lb|en|legal|common law}} Legislated rule of [[society]] which has been given the force of law by those it governs.

